course: dictionary
lesson: 1529
title: Ceremonial
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ceremony is a formal event that is held in a set way. Ceremonial means connected with that kind of event. «The haka is a Māori ceremonial dance with chanting, stamping and fierce faces.» The clues are chanting and fierce faces, which show it is performed in a special, formal way, not like everyday dancing.
explain: Check with the words around it. The haka is used for «welcomes, celebrations, funerals and challenges.» Those are all events with set ways of doing things, so ceremonial fits. Try the swap test: "a ceremonial dance" makes sense, but "a ceremonial sandwich" does not.
explain: Ceremonial can also describe a role. A ceremonial leader has a title and does official duties for show, but does not hold real power. Clues such as "title" or "for show" tell you this is the second meaning, about display and tradition rather than control.
fact: A ceremony is a formal event, often held in a set way.
fact: «Ceremonial» means used in or connected with a ceremony.
fact: «Ceremonially» means in a formal way, like a ceremony.
fact: A ceremonial role can be a title held for show, without real power.
fact: The haka is a Māori ceremonial dance used for welcomes, celebrations, funerals and challenges, not only before battles.
exercise: «The haka is a Māori ceremonial dance with chanting and stamping.» What does ceremonial mean here? | Made of wood | Very fast and silly | *Connected with a formal event | Played only in the rain
exercise: A king can be a ceremonial leader. What does that suggest? | Makes all the laws alone | *Has a title for show, without real power | Lives in a tent | Is the smallest person in the land
exercise: «The guards wore ceremonial robes at the coronation.» Find and copy one word that names a formal event. | robes | wore | guards | *coronation
test: «The royal family attended the ceremonial opening of the bridge.» What does ceremonial mean? | Cheap and old | *Connected with a formal, official event | Made of paper | Very tiny and quiet
test: Which sentence uses ceremonial correctly? | She ceremonial the football down the hill | *The queen carries out ceremonial duties, such as greeting visitors at official events | The ceremonial ate his breakfast quickly and ran to school | The rain was ceremonial and made the grass wet
exam: Jayden reads «a ceremonial leader» and says it means the leader is very bossy. Is he right? | *Right, ceremonial means bossy | Wrong, it means very hungry | Wrong, it means a title held for show, without real power | Right, it means very loud
